 ## Operating characteristics
-
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$, where $N$ is the number of pixels and $S$ is the number of steps per ray. The complexity is linear with respect to resolution and step count [S1, S8, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V)$ for the volume texture, where $V$ is the number of voxels. Additional memory for light density fields or hash tables (in Instant-NGP variants) increases this [S1, S6, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** On an NVIDIA 3090 GPU at 800x800 resolution, the Taichi NGP implementation achieves up to 66 fps [S6, unofficial]. Performance is heavily dependent on the number of steps and the complexity of lighting calculations [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$, where $N$ is the number of pixels and $S$ is the number of steps per ray [S1, S8, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V)$ for the volume texture, plus $O(V)$ for optional light density fields or hash tables [S1, S6, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** Up to 66 fps on an NVIDIA 3090 GPU at 800x800 resolution [S6, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Real-time performance on modern GPUs; supports complex lighting, shadows, and refraction; no need for mesh extraction [S1, S6, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Fixed step size can lead to aliasing (wood-grain artifacts) in low-density regions or high-frequency details; requires careful tuning of step size and transfer functions; memory intensive for high-resolution volumes [S2, S3, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use:** Real-time visualization of smoke, clouds, fluids, and medical data where interactive frame rates are required [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **When Not to Use:** Offline rendering requiring high accuracy with adaptive sampling; scenes with extremely high-frequency density variations that require many steps to resolve [S2, S8, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Fixed step size can cause aliasing (wood-grain artifacts) at low sample counts, mitigated by stochastic jittering [S2, unofficial]. Requires tuning of step size and transfer functions [S10].
+*   **When to Use:** Real-time visualization of smoke, clouds, fluids, and medical data [S1, S2, unofficial].
