 ## Background
-
-Ray Marching Volume Rendering is a fundamental technique in computer graphics for visualizing volumetric data. It is based on the volume rendering integral, which approximates the light transport through a participating medium [S4, S8, unofficial]. The method has been widely implemented in various frameworks, including OpenGL shaders [S3, S5, S9, unofficial], CUDA engines [S7, unofficial], and high-level frameworks like Taichi for real-time applications [S1, S6, unofficial]. The Taichi NGP Renderer specifically adapts the Instant-NGP approach for volume rendering, using hash encoding and fully fused MLPs for density and color prediction, enabling real-time rendering of complex scenes [S6, unofficial]. The technique is commonly used in scientific visualization, visual effects, and real-time fluid simulation [S1, S2, unofficial].
